":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":8,"closed_issues":4466,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-02-14T11:52:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T23:48:31Z","due_on":"2025-03-03T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-03-19T09:35:35Z"},"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-02-15T08:10:03Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T19:08:22Z","closed_at":"2025-02-20T19:08:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4.beta3.\n-  Not reproducible in 4.3.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta3 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-9900KF CPU @ 3.60GHz (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen one_shot is true in a GPUParticles3D node, spawn angle has no effect. If one_shot is false, spawn angle works correctly. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n-Add GPUParrticles3D node\n-Add new particle process material\n- Spawn -> angle -> min 0 to max 360\n- (optional: set acceleration -> gravity to zero for clarity)\n- Add quadmesh as draw pass 1 \n- Add new standard material 3d to material slot in draw pass 1 quadmesh\n- In material, Albedo -> texture -> icon.svg\n- In material, Billboard -> mode -> Particle Billboard (also does not work with particle flags rotate y and disable z per documentation)\n- Back at top, set lifetime to .05 and amount to 1\n- test emitting with both one_shot enabled and disabled and you will see that no random rotation is applied if one_shot = true \n- (not reproducible in 4.3.stable)\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[one_shot_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18809321/one_shot_mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id"